        "text": "Step 2: Next, we use the fact that the point where the altitudes intersect (the orthocenter) forms a cyclic quadrilateral with the vertices of the triangle. This means that the opposite angles of this quadrilateral are supplementary. Specifically, for quadrilateral ABCH, we have:\n\\[\n\\angle AHB + \\angle ACB = 180^\\circ\n\\]"
